---
title: Text replace
tags: tools
heading: "Replace characters"
summary: >-
    Replaces any characters or phrases in text with others. Switch on Regex to use <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regular_expression" class="text-convrtr" title="Regular expression wikipedia page">regex</a> patterns for advanced replacements.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% call toolSection() %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Replace characters", placeholder = "Example: Hello &srarr; lo &srarr; ium &srarr; Helium", actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Replace" }]) %}
<div class="tool-field">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Value">Old<span class="visually-hidden"> characters</span></label>
    <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Value" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
</div>
<div class="tool-field">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}mentValue">New<span class="visually-hidden"> characters</span></label>
    <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}mentValue" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
</div>
{#- Shown while Regex is on, pointing at the pattern and New as they're typed (tools/text/replace.js) #}
<p class="tool-frame__settings-link" id="{{ filename }}Regex101Note" hidden>
    <a href="https://regex101.com/?flavor=javascript" class="text-convrtr" id="{{ filename }}Regex101" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open this pattern in regex101<span class="visually-hidden"> (new tab)</span> <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
</p>
<div class="form-check form-switch">
    <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="{{ filename }}Regex" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}RegexHint">
    <label class="form-check-label" for="{{ filename }}Regex">Regex</label>
</div>
<div class="form-check form-switch">
    <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="{{ filename }}Case">
    <label class="form-check-label" for="{{ filename }}Case">Case sensitive</label>
</div>
{#- Shown while Regex is on (tools/text/replace.js) #}
<div class="tool-frame__note" id="{{ filename }}RegexHint" hidden>
    <p>Patterns use JavaScript's regex, and ^ and $ match at the start and end of each line. In New, $1 is the first group in brackets, $&lt;name&gt; a named group, $&amp; the whole match, and $$ a $ itself.</p>
    <p>To build or test a pattern, try <a href="https://regex101.com/?flavor=javascript" class="text-convrtr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">regex101<span class="visually-hidden"> (new tab)</span></a> with the ECMAScript flavour. "Open this pattern in regex101" opens yours there, sending only the pattern and New, not your text.</p>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
